AB  - Biofertilizers have gained increasing attention as a sustainable alternative to conventional agrochemicals, although the latter remain more widely used in agriculture. Despite its considerable biodiversity and biotechnological potential, Colombia is not a leading producer of biofertilizers, limiting its ability to meet food needs sustainably. This review examines current trends in Colombia’s biofertilizer sector, from the scientific basis for their production to the challenges the country faces in harnessing microbial biodiversity for agriculture. Drawing on a search of indexed databases and an analysis of biofertilizers registered in Colombia, the review considers microbial composition, production methods, market trends, bioproduct composition and formulation, and current regulations. It also explores the future of biofertilizers in Colombia, their potential applications and effects on agricultural production, and approaches to accelerating their development and improving their use and adoption in the country.
